# UST.G3BR H02 Alternate Split-Prime Initializer Theorem v1

## Result

Construct the selected H02 endpoint chart directly over `Z[gamma]` from the frozen characteristic-zero three-block chart oracle and add the exact 19-term G3BI correction update. At the completely split place

```text
(p,gamma) = (21817,5),
```

the resulting `42706 x 42706` sparse chart has determinant

```text
419 mod 21817.
```

This is nonzero. Therefore the selected H02 endpoint chart determinant is a nonzero element of `Z[gamma]`, and the chart is invertible over `Q(gamma)`.

The proof-place chart has 2,328,143 nonzero entries. Its correction update has shape `42706 x 42458` with 118,861 nonzero entries. An independent verifier reconstructs both matrices from the exact source columns and reruns the full sparse determinant elimination.

## Significance

G3BR closes H02 endpoint chart existence, the remaining chart-existence clause left open by G3BN. Together, G3BN and G3BR provide selected `Q(gamma)`-invertible endpoint charts in both H11 and H02. The operator frontier is consequently action evaluation and certified reconstruction, not chart discovery.

## Exact scope

This theorem does not evaluate the H11-to-H02 correction action, reconstruct either inverse over `Q(gamma)`, continue the integral class along G3BJ, or emit the terminal B89 readout. A nonzero modular determinant proves characteristic-zero invertibility but does not provide the inverse coefficients.

